Z||000003||87ECO5||08-17-2001||06:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>Leave Saturday morning, tour the plant, ...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The plant isn't open on Saturday.  Tours are twice/day (one morning, one afternoon) Monday-Friday only.<P>We'd have to leave Friday morning, get there for the afternoon tour, do something that evening, tour the museum Saturday morning and Mammoth Caves Saturday afternoon, party Saturday night, then come home Sunday morning.<P>Hmmm ... I just organized it!  Must come natural or something ...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BENGAL4:<BR><B>BTW, what route are you going to take to get there Drew?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'd suggest 75 to 71 to 65.  That way, if Mike wants to go, he can meet up with us on 65 south of Louisville (like he did when he hooked up with Chad and I before the swap meet).<P>Plus, I bet it's absolutely beautiful in the fall with the leaves changing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||08-17-2001||07:43 PM||||75 to 71 to 65 would be my preferred and always used route. <P>Sorry, "plant" slipped out in my first post. I meant, head down Saturday, tour the museum, etc, etc. I don't plan to skip work on Friday for the trip. Would be a Saturday thing most likely for me. <P><BR>The only times I have been through Cincy in the last 2 years have been to go to Eds and FOCOA nationals last year. But, exceptions have to be made at times  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P><BR>So far, we have Bill with the S/C 3800, Scott with the 3.6L, and me with the soon to be installed fresh 2.9L.<P>No-one else? What about you M7F? Kentucky is closer than Ohio(wow, I have geography skills <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) Just the three of us at this point.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
